s__0047", "ticker": "NVDA", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-01-26", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.4369, "filing_name": "NVIDIA Corporation 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581025000023/nvda-20250126.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "NVDA_10K_2025-01-26__risk_factors__0001", "ticker": "NVDA", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-01-26", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.2781, "filing_name": "NVIDIA Corporation 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581025000023/nvda-20250126.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "NVDA_10K_2025-01-26__risk_factors__0000", "ticker": "NVDA", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-01-26", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.0751, "filing_name": "NVIDIA Corporation 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581025000023/nvda-20250126.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "NVDA_10K_2025-01-26__risk_factors__0046", "ticker": "NVDA", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-01-26", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 0.968, "filing_name": "NVIDIA Corporation 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581025000023/nvda-20250126.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "NVDA_10K_2025-01-26__risk_factors__0016", "ticker": "NVDA", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-01-26", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 0.912, "filing_name": "NVIDIA Corporation 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581025000023/nvda-20250126.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "NVDA_10K_2025-01-26__risk_factors__0015", "ticker": "NVDA", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-01-26", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 0.9115, "filing_name": "NVIDIA Corporation 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581025000023/nvda-20250126.htm", "truncated": false}], "collapsed_near_duplicates": 286, "dropped_candidates": 711, "token_estimate": 31880, "gaps": [], "degraded": []}, "answer": {"direct_answer": "All six companies disclose AI-related risks, but with different emphases. Microsoft, NVIDIA, and Meta describe AI-specific risk factors centered on harmful or flawed outputs, reputational harm, and legal liability [MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__risk_factors__0017] [NVDA_10K_2025-01-26__risk_factors__0047]. Meta also flags AI investment returns and AI-related security vulnerabilities [META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0019] [META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0093]. Alphabet treats AI mainly through ethical and regulatory challenges and as a cyber-attack accelerant [GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0004] [GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0021]. Apple and Amazon mention AI inside broader risks: Apple on safety, privacy, and regulation, and Amazon on competition, investment recovery, and supply constraints [AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0011] [AMZN_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0002]. The chunks do not rank these risks, and the periods differ: Apple, Alphabet, Amazon, and Meta cite 10-Ks for their fiscal 2025, Microsoft cites its 10-K for fiscal 2025 (ended June 30, 2025) plus later 10-Qs, and NVIDIA cites its fiscal 2025 10-K (ended January 26, 2025).", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "AAPL", "company": "Apple Inc", "findings": [{"point": "Apple says new and complex technologies such as AI features can increase safety risks, including exposing users to harmful, inaccurate or other negative content (fiscal 2025, ended September 27, 2025).", "citations": ["AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0011"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Apple says the risk of inadvertent disclosure of personal data can increase with AI features.", "citations": ["AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0029"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Apple lists machine learning and AI among regulated subjects and says regulatory and IP-claim risks may grow as AI is integrated into its products.", "citations": ["AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0023", "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0021"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "MSFT", "company": "Microsoft Corporation", "findings": [{"point": "Microsoft says AI algorithms or training data may be flawed or biased, and AI-generated content may be offensive, illegal, inaccurate, or harmful (10-K, fiscal 2025, ended June 30, 2025).", "citations": ["MSFT_10K_2025-06-30__risk_factors__0017"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Microsoft cites IP, data privacy, product liability, and an evolving global regulatory landscape as sources of AI liability; the Q2 fiscal 2026 10-Q (ended December 31, 2025) adds agentic AI and over-reliance on companion AI.", "citations": ["MSFT_10Q_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0018"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Microsoft says AI is a highly competitive, fast-evolving market where it will bear significant development and operational costs, and that it relies on partner OpenAI among others (Q2 fiscal 2026, ended December 31, 2025).", "citations": ["MSFT_10Q_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0002", "MSFT_10Q_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0017"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "GOOG", "company": "Alphabet Inc", "findings": [{"point": "Alphabet says AI products raise ethical, technological, legal, and regulatory challenges that could harm its brands and demand (fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025).", "citations": ["GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0004"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Alphabet says AI features may be susceptible to unanticipated security threats as understanding of AI-centric security risks develops.", "citations": ["GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0020"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Alphabet says AI development may increase exposure to cyber attacks, including AI used to impersonate senior management.", "citations": ["GOOG_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0021"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "AMZN", "company": "Amazon.com Inc", "findings": [{"point": "Amazon says it may not recoup significant AI investments, which could be written down or written off (fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025).", "citations": ["AMZN_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0002"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Amazon says AI facilitates competitive entry and says constraints on product availability could limit its ability to develop and operate AI.", "citations": ["AMZN_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0001", "AMZN_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0018"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Amazon says its security measures may be circumvented using developing technologies such as AI, and that AI regulation is evolving.", "citations": ["AMZN_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0015", "AMZN_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0024"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "META", "company": "Meta Platforms Inc", "findings": [{"point": "Meta lists AI risks including harmful or illegal content, misinformation, deepfakes, bias, IP infringement, and regulatory scrutiny, and says there is no assurance AI investments will pay off (fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025).", "citations": ["META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0019"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Meta says AI development exposes it to novel vulnerabilities such as prompt injection and compromise of source code and model weights.", "citations": ["META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0093"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Meta names the EU AI Act among the laws it is subject to.", "citations": ["META_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0001"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "NVDA", "company": "NVIDIA Corporation", "findings": [{"point": "NVIDIA says AI solutions with unintended consequences, copyright infringement, or controversial societal impact could cause reputational harm, competitive harm, or legal liability (fiscal 2025, ended January 26, 2025).", "citations": ["NVDA_10K_2025-01-26__risk_fa